Pinkcoin depends: a thinned copy of Gridcoin's depends
=====================================================

This is Gridcoin's depends system (which is Bitcoin Core's, adapted), cut down
to what Pinkcoin builds: static dependencies for two hosts.

  x86_64-pc-linux-gnu    Linux, built natively
  x86_64-w64-mingw32     Windows, cross-built from Linux

    make -C depends HOST=x86_64-pc-linux-gnu -j"$(nproc)"
    make -C depends HOST=x86_64-w64-mingw32  -j"$(nproc)"

Each run leaves depends/<host>/ with the libraries, headers, Qt host tools
(native/bin) and toolchain.cmake. Pass that file to the first CMake call:

    cmake -B build --toolchain depends/<host>/toolchain.cmake

macOS is not built here: the release builds it natively against Homebrew.
README.md, description.md and packages.md are Gridcoin's documentation,
unchanged; parts of them describe hosts and packages this copy drops.

Where each file came from
-------------------------

Taken with `git archive` (tracked files only, no build output):

  HEAD   Gridcoin-Research development at 2d4e644386 (2026-11-08); its
         depends/ last changed in 9fe993b58c (2026-10-27).
  1ceea  Gridcoin-Research 1ceea8397e (2023-07-13), "build: Bump Qt to
         5.15.5 in depends", Gridcoin's last Qt 5 recipe (Qt 6 support came
         in aaac3ee843).
  BC29   Bitcoin Core v29.2 (2d6426c296, 2025-10-10), its last Qt 5 release
         series.

  From HEAD, unchanged:
    .gitignore config.guess config.sub gen_id README.md description.md
    packages.md builders/{default,linux,darwin}.mk
    hosts/{default,linux,mingw32}.mk
    packages/{openssl,zlib,qrencode,miniupnpc,expat,libXau,xproto,
      libxcb_util,libxcb_util_render,libxcb_util_keysyms,libxcb_util_wm}.mk
    patches/boost/skip_compiled_targets.patch
    patches/fontconfig/gperf_header_regen.patch (identical at 1ceea)
    patches/miniupnpc/dont_leak_info.patch
  From HEAD, changed (see below):
    Makefile funcs.mk toolchain.cmake.in packages/boost.mk
  From 1ceea, unchanged:
    packages/freetype.mk, patches/qt/* (12 files; no_sdk_version_check.patch
    is not applied by qt.mk, as at 1ceea)
  From 1ceea, changed (see below):
    packages/{qt,libxcb,fontconfig,libxkbcommon,libxcb_util_image}.mk
  From BC29, unchanged:
    packages/xcb_proto.mk
  New:
    packages/packages.mk (the package lists), README.pink2

  Removed from Pinkcoin's tree: the 2.4.0.0 leftovers
  patches/fontconfig/{gperf_header_regen,remove_char_width_usage}.patch, which
  no build used. Gridcoin's fontconfig recipe applies its own
  gperf_header_regen.patch (a different patch, for fontconfig 2.12.6), which
  now sits at that path.

Packages and versions
---------------------

  all hosts    boost 1.89.0, openssl 3.5.9, zlib 1.3.1, qrencode 4.1.1,
               miniupnpc 2.2.2, qt 5.15.5 (qtbase, qttools, qttranslations,
               qtsvg)
  Linux only   expat 2.4.8, libxcb 1.14, xcb_proto 1.15.2, libXau 1.0.9,
               xproto 7.0.31, freetype 2.11.0, fontconfig 2.12.6,
               libxkbcommon 0.8.4, libxcb_util 0.4.0,
               libxcb_util_render 0.3.9, libxcb_util_keysyms 0.4.0,
               libxcb_util_image 0.4.0, libxcb_util_wm 0.4.1
  native       none

Every tarball is checked against the sha256 in its .mk.

Versions and recipes that differ from Gridcoin's current tree
-------------------------------------------------------------

  qt            5.15.5 (Gridcoin: 6.7.3). Pinkcoin is Qt 5 only; Qt 6 is a
                separate PR. Recipe from 1ceea.
  libxcb        1.14 (Gridcoin: 1.17.0), 1ceea's recipe: shared library.
  xcb_proto     1.15.2 (Gridcoin: 1.17.0), BC29's recipe.
  fontconfig    same version, 1ceea's recipe: shared library.
  freetype      same version, 1ceea's recipe: shared library.
  libxkbcommon  same version, 1ceea's recipe: shared library.
  libxcb_util_image
                same version, 1ceea's recipe: shared library.

Why. Gridcoin's current X11 recipes build static archives (1ba34e82ba,
written for Qt 6's CMake build). Qt 5.15.5's configure takes each library's
link line from plain `pkg-config --libs` on Linux: its `--static` rerun only
fires when a library resolves to a .a path, and qtConfResolveLibs never does
that on Linux. With the current recipes:

  - Qt's xcb test fails at configure time: libxcb.a needs -lXau, which only
    `pkg-config --static --libs xcb` gives (undefined reference to
    XauGetBestAuthByAddr).
  - fontconfig and xkbcommon-x11 pass configure, but Qt would record the
    plain lines in its .prl files, and Pinkcoin's link would then fail:
    libfontconfig.a needs -lexpat (11 undefined XML_* symbols), and
    xkbcommon-x11 needs -lxcb-xkb -lxcb -lXau.
  - The current libxkbcommon recipe also depends on xkeyboard-config, which
    is not in this package list.

So libxcb, fontconfig and libxkbcommon use 1ceea's recipes, which build
shared libraries, as Gridcoin built Qt 5.15.5 and as BC29 still does. freetype
goes with fontconfig: at run time the GUI loads the system's libfontconfig,
which loads the system's FreeType, and Qt hands its FreeType faces to
fontconfig, so a static FreeType inside the GUI would put two in one process.

libxcb 1.14 then needs an older xcb-proto. With 1.17.0 its generator fails
(KeyError: 'xcb_redirect_t' writing composite.c). 1ceea's 1.14.1 fails to
install on Python 3.12 or later (its automake py-compile imports `imp`).
1.15.2 is BC29's pairing with libxcb 1.14 and installs on Python 3.13.

With libxcb shared, xcb-util-image is the one static xcb-util archive that
still fails: libxcb-image.a needs libxcb-util (xcb_aux_create_gc), which
Qt's configure never records, so a static Qt application does not link. It
uses 1ceea's recipe too (shared, with libxcb-util inside).

The other X11 recipes stay current. The static xcb-util, xcb-util-renderutil,
xcb-util-keysyms and xcb-util-wm archives link from their plain .pc lines
(Gridcoin's recipes add -lXau there), expat is only linked into depends'
libfontconfig.so, and libXau and xproto were static and header-only at 1ceea
too.

Consequence: Pinkcoin-Qt on Linux loads libxcb (and its extension
libraries), libxcb-image, libxkbcommon(-x11), libfontconfig and libfreetype
from the system at run time, the model of every Qt 5 depends build. pink2d
does not link any of them.

Changes from the sources, and why
---------------------------------

packages/packages.mk
  packages boost openssl zlib; qt_packages qrencode; upnp_packages miniupnpc;
  qt_mingw32_packages qt; qt_linux_packages qt expat libxcb xcb_proto libXau
  xproto freetype fontconfig libxkbcommon libxcb_util libxcb_util_render
  libxcb_util_keysyms libxcb_util_image libxcb_util_wm. No native packages:
  nothing here needs ccache or xxd.

packages/qt.mk (1ceea's, with these changes)
  - download path: download.qt.io/archive/qt/5.15/5.15.5/submodules. 5.15.5
    is no longer under official_releases (404); the archive serves the same
    tarballs, by the same sha256.
  - extra_sources lists the qtsvg tarball (it named an unset variable, so the
    source check skipped qtsvg; the extract step checked it anyway).
  - GIF support is kept (no -no-gif): Pinkcoin's sync spinner is
    res/movies/update_spinner.gif, played with QMovie.
  - QColorDialog is kept (no -no-feature-colordialog): src/qt/plugins/
    mrichtexteditor/mrichtextedit.cpp uses it, and the header refuses to
    compile with the feature off.
  - -no-feature-gssapi and -no-tslib: otherwise configure finds Kerberos
    GSSAPI and tslib in the build machine's /usr and links them. Nothing in
    Pinkcoin uses either.
  - -bundled-xcb-xinput (Linux): libxcb is built with --disable-xinput (as
    at 1ceea), so configure otherwise compiles against the build machine's
    xcb/xinput.h and links its libxcb-xinput.so. Qt's bundled copy is used
    instead.
  - CMake packages. Pinkcoin uses find_package(Qt5 ... Widgets Network Svg
    LinguistTools), and 1ceea's recipe served pkg-config users only:
      * postprocess keeps lib/cmake/, native/mkspecs/ and the .prl files
        (1ceea deleted them). Qt's static CMake packages read their link
        dependencies from the .prl files, and Qt5::Core's include directories
        point into native/mkspecs/.
      * the stage step also installs qtbase's mkspecs (install_mkspecs) and
        native/bin/qmake (sub-qmake-qmake-aux-pro-install_subtargets):
        Qt5Core's CMake package refuses to load without either.
      * qmake also runs on qttools/src/linguist/linguist.pro, which writes
        lib/cmake/Qt5LinguistTools/*, and the stage step installs only those
        files (install_cmake_linguist_tools_files). Only lrelease, lupdate
        and lconvert are built, as at 1ceea.
  Everything else (configure options, patches, the build of qtbase, qtsvg,
  qttranslations and the three linguist tools) is 1ceea's.

packages/libxcb.mk, packages/fontconfig.mk, packages/libxcb_util_image.mk
(1ceea's)
  - --libdir=<prefix>/lib, the line Gridcoin's current recipes carry. A
    build machine whose config.site moves the default libdir to lib64
    (openSUSE) otherwise installs the .pc files where pkg-config does not
    look. Gridcoin added this in 9eec6909a1 (2021); the 1ceea recipes had
    lost it.

packages/libxkbcommon.mk (1ceea's)
  - -Wno-error=array-bounds, the line Gridcoin's current recipe carries.
    GCC 12 and later flag src/xkbcomp/ast-build.c, and 0.8.4 builds with
    -Werror.

packages/boost.mk (HEAD's)
  - depends on zlib only (bzip2 and xz are dropped), and Boost.Iostreams is
    configured with BZip2, LZMA and Zstd off so that it cannot pick up the
    build machine's libraries.
  - BOOST_INCLUDE_LIBRARIES is Pinkcoin's set: the libraries src/ includes or
    links (filesystem, program_options, thread, chrono and test are
    compiled; the rest are headers). Gridcoin's list has no program_options
    or spirit.

Makefile (HEAD's)
  - the multiprocess (Cap'n Proto) hooks are removed, with their packages.
  - download-osx is removed from `make download` (no darwin host here).
  - the closing message says Pinkcoin.

toolchain.cmake.in (HEAD's)
  - the multiprocess block is removed. The Darwin blocks are inert for these
    two hosts and stay as Gridcoin has them.

funcs.mk (HEAD's)
  - the configure, build and stage lines lose their '+' prefix when make
    runs with -n. GNU make runs '+' lines even under -n, so on a fresh tree
    `make -n` executed them before anything was extracted, and the failed
    'cd' left them running in depends/ itself (zlib's `cmake -S ..` then
    configured Pinkcoin's own CMakeLists.txt). Now `make -n` only prints. A
    normal build is unchanged.

Dropped from Gridcoin's tree
----------------------------

  Packages: capnp, native_capnp, native_libmultiprocess, libevent, curl,
  bzip2, xz, pcre2, harfbuzz, libpng, libXdmcp, libxcb_util_cursor, libICE,
  libSM, util-macros, xkeyboard-config, native_qt, qt_details.mk,
  native_ccache, native_xxd, native_ds_store, native_mac_alias,
  native_libdmg-hfsplus, and Gridcoin's Qt 6 qt.mk. libzip, which 1ceea had,
  is not here either.
  Hosts: darwin (hosts/darwin.mk). Android and FreeBSD hosts were never in
  Gridcoin's tree. builders/darwin.mk stays: it describes a Mac as the
  build machine, not a host.
  Patches: Gridcoin's Qt 6 patches/qt/* (fix-gcc16-*, qtbase_*,
  rcc_hardcode_timestamp; 1ceea's set replaces them), native_biplist,
  native_cdrkit, native_libdmg-hfsplus.
  config.site.in: the CMake-only Makefile no longer generates config.site.

Notes for users of this tree
----------------------------

  - Qt 5's static CMake packages call find_library() for every -l in their
    .prl files (m, dl, ...). toolchain.cmake sets
    CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_LIBRARY ONLY, which hides the system's libm,
    so find_package(Qt5) fails with "Library not found: m". The consumer
    sets the mode to BOTH around find_package(Qt5) only, as Bitcoin Core
    v29's cmake/module/FindQt.cmake does.
  - Static Qt plugins must be linked and imported by the application
    (Qt5::QXcbIntegrationPlugin, Qt5::QGifPlugin, Qt5::QSvgPlugin,
    Qt5::QSvgIconPlugin with Q_IMPORT_PLUGIN). The Qt 4 codec plugins that
    src/qt/bitcoin.cpp imports under BITCOIN_NEED_QT_PLUGINS do not exist in
    Qt 5; the codecs are built into QtCore.
  - Qt is configured with -no-openssl and -no-feature-http (1ceea), so the
    overview page's HTTPS price request gets no reply.
  - Source fallback: FALLBACK_DOWNLOAD_PATHS is Gridcoin's, bitcoincore.org's
    depends-sources first, then Gridcoin's S3 mirror.
  - After a failed build, remove depends/<host>/.<package>_stamp_configured
    (or `make -C depends HOST=<host> clean`) before building again. That
    stamp is named by package, not by build id, so a stale one makes the
    next run skip configure for a new version (upstream behaviour).
  - Gridcoin's funcs.mk runs `xargs $(build_TOUCH)` while caching a package,
    and no builder defines build_TOUCH, so xargs only echoes the file list.
    Harmless; kept as Gridcoin has it.
  - The libraries are built with -std=c++17 (CXX_STANDARD, as Gridcoin), and
    Qt with -c++std c++17. toolchain.cmake puts -std=c++17 in
    CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_INIT; Pinkcoin's CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 11 adds -std=c++11
    after it, and the last one wins.
